{
 "source": "frames_events.png",
 "notes": [
  "The festivals' own frames (balance/cosmetics.json frames/event_<theme>; each festival's last milestone gives its frame): frames_events.png's rows 3, 4 and 5 -- a frame woven of golden wheat sheaves with lanterns at its corners (the Harvest Festival), a blackened iron frame with a crimson moon and blood-red enamel (the Blood Moon), carved wood and striped merchant canvas with brass lanterns and a coin purse (the Merchant Caravan) -- each painted as a square (left) and a ring (right) on the sheet's flat navy, keyed off it as frames_cosmetic_a.json's are (darkkey against the sheet's own ground [9,21,31], k 38, floor 4); the EMPTY windows key clear, so a portrait drawn under a frame shows through. Rows 1, 2 and 6 (the throne's, the court's lion banners, the war's axes) belong to Waves 5 and 8 and are not cut.",
  "frames/event_<theme>_square and _ring at this sheet's own scales, set as frames_cosmetic_a.json's and frames_noble.json's were: every square's plain band 160 across (painted 273: the median of the sheet's six, measured along each window's centre lines) and every ring's 96 (painted 231: the median outer circle on the diagonals, clear of the ornaments on the axes), so a festival's frame is the same size on a portrait as every other frame, its lanterns, moon and purse standing outside the band. _tile is the ring whole in the wardrobe's 224x190 art box; looks/event_<theme>_ring_large the same ring at band 132 (the rankings podium's rings).",
  "Each crop is centred on its frame's own window -- a square's from its inner edges along the centre lines clear of the middle ornaments, a ring's from a circle fitted to its inner edge on the diagonals -- and masked to a polygon round its own ink, grown 3 px and kept off a neighbour's: the blood moon's frame is painted in pieces that come within a pixel or two of the harvest's above and the caravan's below, so the ink is labelled unclosed and every piece given to the cell its centre falls in. Written by a measuring script (fork B's scratchpad forkB/gen_frames_events.py, fork D's gen_frames_noble.py with this sheet's rows): its numbers, not hand-read ones."
 ],
